1
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:34,665
Once, in this very town, there was a sweet shop that opened only at midnight.

2
00:00:39,025 --> 00:00:41,539
And you could not pay with money there.

3
00:00:41,925 --> 00:00:43,790
Only with goodness.

4
00:00:44,942 --> 00:00:46,504
Then what happened?

5
00:00:49,842 --> 00:00:55,617
Then... hm. The ending's gone again. Like a sweet you left in your pocket.

6
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:59,949
Because there is no ending. It's made up.

7
00:02:14,292 --> 00:02:16,338
It's just a wall, Chutney.

8
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:08,214
You're late.

9
00:03:12,975 --> 00:03:14,744
Eighty years late.

10
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,590
I'm only nine.

11
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:22,579
Then you're very early for someone so late.

12
00:03:33,517 --> 00:03:36,233
Floating laddoo. Very popular.

13
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,217
I don't have any money.

14
00:03:43,458 --> 00:03:44,601
Money?

15
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:46,258
Hee hee hee hee!

16
00:03:47,608 --> 00:03:49,613
We don't take money here.

17
00:03:49,808 --> 00:03:52,184
Tola weighs something heavier.

18
00:03:54,150 --> 00:03:56,197
Put your hand on the pan.

19
00:03:56,350 --> 00:04:00,042
Think of one kind thing you did today. A true one.

20
00:04:26,758 --> 00:04:30,763
One floating laddoo. It lasts until first light.

21
00:04:31,833 --> 00:04:33,787
Not one minute more.

22
00:05:54,125 --> 00:05:55,999
You were floating. I saw you.

23
00:06:12,667 --> 00:06:14,563
If this is a joke—

24
00:06:35,692 --> 00:06:37,677
I'll have the best thing you've got.

25
00:06:38,625 --> 00:06:40,050
Pay first.

26
00:06:42,333 --> 00:06:47,687
Today I saved a whole busload of children from a flood. With a rope. And a helicopter.

27
00:06:55,525 --> 00:06:56,818
It's broken.

28
00:07:10,692 --> 00:07:16,214
Tola only weighs what's true, little man. Come back when you've done something real.

29
00:07:20,258 --> 00:07:23,804
It's a stupid shop anyway. A stupid sugar museum.

30
00:07:28,925 --> 00:07:32,662
That one's hungry for something. And it isn't sweets.

31
00:09:16,392 --> 00:09:24,579
You gave me your water when you were thirsty too, so I'll guard you forever... also I ate your slipper last week. Sorry.

32
00:09:50,942 --> 00:09:53,182
Amma, where are all the sweets going?

33
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:56,551
Oh, sweets come, sweets go.

34
00:10:45,542 --> 00:10:46,552
Show us!

35
00:10:47,425 --> 00:10:50,699
Wish jalebis. One coil, one wish. Watch this.

36
00:10:52,342 --> 00:10:55,636
I wish this gali was the sweetest place in the world!

37
00:11:10,375 --> 00:11:13,148
I wish I had the fastest ride in town!

38
00:11:29,133 --> 00:11:30,724
Make the buffalo pretty!

39
00:12:10,475 --> 00:12:12,500
Gloves? In this heat?

40
00:12:14,233 --> 00:12:15,470
It's... fashion.

41
00:13:04,167 --> 00:13:05,925
Ah. Both of you.

42
00:13:09,267 --> 00:13:12,668
I took it. I wanted them to think I was... somebody.

43
00:13:20,217 --> 00:13:21,435
I'm sorry.

44
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:26,194
Oh, little man.

45
00:13:28,808 --> 00:13:30,503
Then take my sorry.

46
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:47,487
Amma, why are you fading?

47
00:13:49,642 --> 00:13:54,867
A shop like this lives in people's remembering. When the last one forgets...

48
00:13:57,117 --> 00:13:59,261
...poof. Sugar in the rain.

49
00:14:04,025 --> 00:14:08,259
Nani's story. She forgot the ending... and you started to fade.

50
00:14:10,492 --> 00:14:11,991
Who's Nani?

51
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:16,357
We need Nani.

52
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,865
Nani. Wake up. It's your story. It's real.

53
00:14:39,417 --> 00:14:42,458
At my age? Down all those stairs?

54
00:14:44,708 --> 00:14:46,225
I'll take you, Nani.

55
00:15:04,083 --> 00:15:06,179
One more, Nani. I've got you.

56
00:15:50,033 --> 00:15:53,330
I was the girl. I was the girl in the story.

57
00:16:14,283 --> 00:16:16,239
There you are, Sharda.

58
00:16:18,392 --> 00:16:20,056
I forgot you.

59
00:16:22,017 --> 00:16:25,988
Everybody forgets. The trick is remembering again.

60
00:16:47,350 --> 00:16:49,313
Now that... is heavy.

61
00:17:17,358 --> 00:17:20,570
The job of remembering. It's yours now.

62
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:24,577
Will you be here next summer?

63
00:17:25,708 --> 00:17:28,431
If somebody tells the story right.

64
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,636
Don't let the story lose its ending.

65
00:18:44,675 --> 00:18:49,035
...and the shop stayed, as long as someone remembered it. That's the ending.

66
00:19:03,567 --> 00:19:06,845
Well. That's how it ends. And that's how it begins.
